WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.566
This example begins with price and quantity stored
as strings They look like numbers to

00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:11.987
us but Python still sees text because the values are
inside quotation marks The

00:00:12.001 --> 00:00:16.922
float conversion turns the price into a decimal
number and the integer conversion turns the

00:00:16.948 --> 00:00:22.806
quantity into a whole number After conversion Python
can multiply them to calculate

00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:28.479
the total Run the example and then change the
quantity text from five

00:00:28.506 --> 00:00:34.193
to eight Notice that conversion is not only a
technical detail It

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:38.732
determines whether the data can participate
correctly in a numerical calculation
